When :func:`icalendar.use_pytz` was in effect, a date parsed with a ``TZID``, such as ``RDATE;TZID=America/New_York;VALUE=DATE:19970101``, was given the timezone's oldest known offset, its local mean time, so the value was minutes off. It is now read with the offset that applied on that date. Calendars read with zoneinfo, the default, were not affected. I used AI to assist me with this change. @lcampanella98
